  "plan": {
    "goal": "Bypass the croc, now at (48,6), by going NW to (33,5), then N up column 33/34 to row 0, then step N into zone 11.21.0.0.",
    "guidance": "If there is no combat, follow the NW diagonal to (33,5), continue N to row 0, and step N. The croc is hostile and 9 cells away; keep W/NW of it. If it comes within 4, keep moving W/NW on land away from the open water at x10-28. Fight only if the croc is adjacent and there is no escape. Dragonflies, glowfish and glowpads are neutral.",
    "memory": "Joppa is JoppaWorld.11.22.1.1.10; Mehmet was seen at (42,19). Accepted quest 'What's Eating the Watervine?': go to Red Rock (world 11,20), kill a spider-like vermin and bring its corpse back to Mehmet. I am lost, so there is no fast travel; I am walking N zone by zone. Now in 11.21.1 (salt marsh); next is 11.21.0, then parcel 11,20. In 11.21.1, a hostile croc was seen from turn 101 to 102 at (47,6)-(50,5), moving back and forth; it has not engaged. Open water is at x10-28 y11-24. Land along the route (38,10)-(33,5)-(33,3) is displayed but unverified. I have not done the water ritual. Albino: slow regeneration in daylight. My only healing is witchwood bark, which confuses.",
